    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required rejecting a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date with a 400 response.\n\nI added a single new class, `OwnerRegistrationDateAdvice`, following the existing per-rule `@ControllerAdvice` / `RequestBodyAdvice` pattern used by the other owner validation rules (postcode, telephone length, city capacity, etc.). It:\n\n- hooks only the `addOwner` create endpoint,\n- checks `OwnerFieldsDto.getRegistrationDate()` and throws when it `isAfter(LocalDate.now())` (an absent date is left alone, since it later defaults to the server date),\n- maps that exception to `400 Bad Request`.\n\n**Structural impact:** one file touched, no existing function modified. Every method in the new class has minimal cyclomatic complexity and near-zero surrounding WMC_other, so the cost formula stays small \u2014 behaviour was added as a cohesive new unit rather than by growing an existing method or class.",
